      "endVerse": 0,
      "author": "Tried By Fire",
      "authorHandle": "@TriedByFire",
      "text": "If you like simple, down-to-earth, easily understood, fluffy rainbows and unicorn books of the Bible, you are certainly not going to find it here. Honestly, you probably won’t find it much of the Bible. Every way you look in scripture, there is some sort of issue that faithful men face. If it’s not Jacob facing the daunting task of pleasing his wives, or his children literally trying to kill one of his sons, or David facing battles and fleshly lusts with Bathsheba (Solomon’s—the supposed author of this book—mother), or you go ahead and pick your character, Solomon has an interesting approach to this book of the Bible as far as setting the tone.",
