      "chapter": 1,
      "verse": 0,
      "startVerse": 0,
      "endVerse": 0,
      "author": "Tried By Fire",
      "authorHandle": "@TriedByFire",
      "text": "Thirdly, we should establish (by the end of this) what the ultimate purpose of this book is for. We will start off by addressing HOW we should focus this book, and where we should focus this book, but it should conclude with the answer and solution for utilizing this book of the Bible. I don’t think I’ve ever heard but maybe one sermon from this book of the Bible. It’s rich with great advice and practical, easy-to-use thoughts for when things are looking quite bleak either in your life, or (rather especially) in your faith. We are going to walk through valleys a lot more often than standing on mountain tops. There will be mountain top times, but they won’t be as numerous as the dark valleys we have to tread because this Earth (as long as we are here) is a very dark and cruel place.",
