      "book": "Ecclesiastes",
      "chapter": 1,
      "verse": 6,
      "startVerse": 6,
      "endVerse": 7,
      "author": "Tried By Fire",
      "authorHandle": "@TriedByFire",
      "text": "The sun is the most predictable out of all these cycles. Rain isn’t. Wind isn’t. We can’t depend on those things. God will provide them in His own timing. There are people who try to figure it out, but they never will. They are literally chasing the wind. How much more vain can you get? I think the literal definition of vanity should be “Chasing the wind.”",
      "likes": 0,
      "isLikedByUser": false,
      "isBookmarkedByUser": false,
