          "book": "Ecclesiastes",
          "chapter": 1,
          "verse": 0,
          "startVerse": 0,
          "endVerse": 0,
          "author": "Tried By Fire",
          "authorHandle": "@TriedByFire",
          "text": "Secondly, we need to establish the tone. The tone shifts up and down throughout each chapter. The author will talk about highlights of his life, the amount of work he has had to go through to get there, and what he has found some fleeting joy in for the time being while he works. He also talks (quite heavily) about how none of it actually even matters in the end anyway because it will all just be taken away or abused. His hard work will go to someone else. This, to me anyway, sets the tone for MOST (if not ALL) of God’s faithful members throughout all of scripture. Including Jesus Christ, they all have some sort of difficult battle they have to face and they feel completely defeated by it.",
